{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T23:33:21.671Z","data":{"text":"Task 5 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the mutation reporting and show output for change 083, following TDD (tests written first, then implementation).\n\n**New module** `src/core/report/report-mutation.ts`: reads numbered task event streams across active and archived changes, keeps the latest measured `mutation_ran` event per `<file>#<function>` by timestamp, groups by opted-in capabilities named in each event's `scenarios`, and returns killed/survived sums, a 3-decimal score (null for 0/0), and survivors. `formatMutation` renders the text section.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `report.ts`: `MetricsReport.mutation?`, `getMetricsReport` fills it, `formatMetricsReport` prints it only when present.\n- `cli/report.ts`: `toStableMetrics` copies it only when present, with the exact stable JSON shape.\n- `show.ts`: `formatMutationRuns` beside `formatFocusedRuns` emits `Mutation:` and `Survived:` lines after `Focused runs:`, using only events after the last `measures` start.\n- `README.md`: new `### Mutation checks` subsection covering config, picks, ranges/tests, placeholders/env vars, budget, not-measured reasons, the event, show/report lines, and the reference StrykerJS setup with the exact `stryker.config.mjs`.\n\n**Tests:** new `tests/mutation-report.test.ts` (9 tests) covers both requirements' scenarios plus grouping, filtering, and ordering edge cases through `getMetricsReport`, the report command (text + JSON), and `getSpecDetailsFromFolder`/`formatSpecDetails`.\n\n**Verification:** task `verify` passes (9/9), `tests/report-json.test.ts` and `fixture/report/expected.json` pass unchanged, lint is clean, and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, UI + CLI build, full suite, lint) passes.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/083-traceability-mutation/.run/results/5.md`."}}
